# Formatting Guidelines

**Code formatting standards for consistent, clean code presentation.**

## **JSX Formatting**

- **Don't add empty spaces in JSX return** - Keep components and HTML tags compact
- **No unnecessary blank lines between JSX elements**
- **Maintain consistent indentation and structure**

```tsx
// ✅ DO: Compact JSX without unnecessary spacing
const MyComponent = () => (
  <div>
    <header>
      <h1>Title</h1>
      <nav>Navigation</nav>
    </header>
    <main>
      <section>Content</section>
      <aside>Sidebar</aside>
    </main>
    <footer>Footer</footer>
  </div>
);

// ❌ DON'T: Unnecessary spacing in JSX
const MyComponent = () => (
  <div>
    <header>
      <h1>Title</h1>

      <nav>Navigation</nav>
    </header>

    <main>
      <section>Content</section>

      <aside>Sidebar</aside>
    </main>

    <footer>Footer</footer>
  </div>
);
```

## **Code Spacing and Organization**

- **Add blank lines for logical grouping** - Between imports, constants, types, and main code blocks
- **Group related code together** without internal spacing
- **Separate different logical sections** with single blank lines

```ts
// ✅ DO: Proper logical grouping
import { useState, useEffect } from 'react'
import { slugify } from '~utils/slugify'

const API_ENDPOINTS = {
  users: '/api/users',
  posts: '/api/posts'
}

const DEFAULT_CONFIG = { timeout: 5000, retries: 3 }

type Props = {
  userId: string
  onUpdate: (data: any) => void
}

const UserProfile = ({ userId, onUpdate }: Props) => {
  const [user, setUser] = useState(null)
  const [loading, setLoading] = useState(true)

  const fetchUser = async () => {
    setLoading(true)
    const response = await fetch(`${API_ENDPOINTS.users}/${userId}`)
    const userData = await response.json()
    setUser(userData)
    setLoading(false)
  }

  useEffect(() => {
    fetchUser()
  }, [userId])

  return <div>{loading ? <div>Loading...</div> : <div>{user?.name}</div>}</div>
}

// ❌ DON'T: Poor spacing and grouping
import { useState, useEffect } from 'react'

import { slugify } from '~utils/slugify'
const API_ENDPOINTS = {
  users: '/api/users',
  posts: '/api/posts'
}

const DEFAULT_CONFIG = { timeout: 5000, retries: 3 }
type Props = {
  userId: string
  onUpdate: (data: any) => void
}
const UserProfile = ({ userId, onUpdate }: Props) => {
  const [user, setUser] = useState(null)

  const [loading, setLoading] = useState(true)
  const fetchUser = async () => {
    setLoading(true)

    const response = await fetch(`${API_ENDPOINTS.users}/${userId}`)

    const userData = await response.json()
    setUser(userData)

    setLoading(false)
  }
  useEffect(() => {
    fetchUser()
  }, [userId])
  return <div>{loading ? <div>Loading...</div> : <div>{user?.name}</div>}</div>
}
```

## **Comments Policy**

- **Don't add comments unless explicitly requested**
- **Keep code self-documenting** through clear naming and structure
- **Focus on clean, readable code** over explanatory comments
- **When comments are needed, make them concise and meaningful**

```ts
// ✅ DO: Self-documenting code without comments
const calculateDiscountedPrice = (
  originalPrice: number,
  discountPercent: number,
) => {
  const discountAmount = originalPrice * (discountPercent / 100);
  return originalPrice - discountAmount;
};

const isValidEmail = (email: string) =>
  /^[^\s@]+@[^\s@]+\.[^\s@]+$/.test(email);

// ❌ DON'T: Unnecessary comments
const calculateDiscountedPrice = (
  originalPrice: number,
  discountPercent: number,
) => {
  // Calculate the discount amount
  const discountAmount = originalPrice * (discountPercent / 100);
  // Subtract discount from original price
  return originalPrice - discountAmount;
};

// Check if email is valid
const isValidEmail = (email: string) =>
  /^[^\s@]+@[^\s@]+\.[^\s@]+$/.test(email); // Email regex pattern
```

## **Consistent Formatting Rules**

- **Use consistent indentation** (2 spaces)
- **Keep line lengths reasonable** (prefer breaking long lines)
- **Use trailing commas** in objects and arrays for cleaner diffs
- **Consistent quote usage** (prefer single quotes)

```ts
// ✅ DO: Consistent formatting
const userConfig = {
  name: "John Doe",
  email: "john@example.com",
  preferences: {
    theme: "dark",
    notifications: true,
    language: "en",
  },
  roles: ["user", "moderator"],
};

// ❌ DON'T: Inconsistent formatting
const userConfig = {
  name: "John Doe",
  email: "john@example.com",
  preferences: {
    theme: "dark",
    notifications: true,
    language: "en",
  },
  roles: ["user", "moderator"],
};
```

**Follow these formatting standards for consistent, readable code across the entire codebase.**
